<description>
Crop out the interior of the largest complete monochrome rectangular frame.

Input structure
A noisy grid contains a closed one-cell-thick rectangular frame whose border
is one color; the desired image is inside that frame.

Rule
Find every monochrome rectangular border, require a unique largest one by
interior area, and return the subgrid strictly inside its border.

Key insight
The frame color is identified by the closed rectangle it forms, not by its
numeric color id; the output is the unchanged frame interior.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "unique largest closed monochrome rectangular frame in the noisy grid",
  "transform": "discard the frame border and all pixels outside it; keep the unchanged pixels strictly inside the frame",
  "grid_shape": "crop to the frame interior"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 13-23 rows x 16-21 cols
  frame:
    shape: closed 1-cell-thick monochrome rectangle
    interior: 5-8 rows x 3-10 cols (>=3 in each dimension)
    color: a single color used ONLY on the frame border, never inside or outside
    position: fully contained in grid; margin >=0 on each side, at least 2 sides have margin >=2
    uniqueness: must be the unique largest monochrome rectangular frame by interior area
  noise:
    region: all cells outside the frame (including frame border cells are frame-colored, not noise)
    colors: same palette as interior (3-4 non-frame, non-zero colors + color 0)
    density: 57-73% non-zero pixels outside frame [observed]
  interior:
    colors: 3-4 non-zero colors + color 0 (same set used in noise region)
    density: 66-73% non-zero [observed]
    content: random fill, no deliberate structure
  total_colors: 5-6 (1 frame + 4-5 content/noise colors including 0)
  output: the interior subgrid (strictly inside the frame border), unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick interior dims H_int in [5,8], W_int in [3,10].
    2. Pick 3-4 non-zero content colors + color 0 to form the palette (4-5 colors total).
    3. Fill the H_int x W_int interior randomly from the content palette (including 0).
    4. Pick 1 frame color not in the content palette.
    5. Build the frame border around the interior (outer size = (H_int+2) x (W_int+2)).
    6. Choose grid dims H >= H_int+4, W >= W_int+4 (range 13-23 x 16-21) ensuring margin >=1 on all sides.
    7. Place the frame at a random valid position with margin >=1 on each side.
    8. Fill all cells outside the frame with random noise from the content palette (same colors as interior).
    9. Verify no accidental monochrome rectangle outside has larger interior area than the main frame; if so, re-randomize noise.
    10. Output = the interior subgrid from step 3.
```
